# API Communication Patterns

## API Client Configuration

### Axios Instance Setup

Located in `src/lib/api/client.ts`:

- Single axios instance for all API calls
- Base URL from environment variable
- Timeout: 30 seconds
- `withCredentials: true` for JWT cookie handling
- Request/response interceptors attached

**Never create new axios instances** - always use the configured `apiClient`.

```typescript
import apiClient from '@/lib/api/client';

// Good
const { data } = await apiClient.get('/users');

// Bad - don't do this
import axios from 'axios';
const { data } = await axios.get('http://localhost:8000/users');
```

## API Endpoints

### Centralized Endpoint Constants

All API endpoints defined in `src/lib/api/endpoints.ts`:

```typescript
export const API_ENDPOINTS = {
  AUTH: {
    LOGIN: '/auth/login',
    LOGOUT: '/auth/logout',
    ME: '/auth/me',
  },
  USERS: {
    LIST: '/users',
    DETAIL: (id: string) => `/users/${id}`,
    CREATE: '/users',
    UPDATE: (id: string) => `/users/${id}`,
    DELETE: (id: string) => `/users/${id}`,
  },
} as const;
```

**Rules:**

- Group by resource (AUTH, USERS, JOBS, etc.)
- Use functions for dynamic segments
- Never hardcode endpoint strings in components or hooks
- Mark as `const` for type safety

## Proxy Pattern

### Next.js API Routes as Proxy

**Critical: Never call FastAPI directly from client**

All API calls go through Next.js API routes first:

- Client calls `/api/users` (Next.js)
- Next.js forwards to `http://fastapi-backend/users`
- Cookies are forwarded automatically
- Response returned to client

This is implemented in `app/api/[...path]/route.ts`.

### Why Use Proxy?

1. **Security**: Hides actual backend URL
2. **Flexibility**: Can change backend without changing client
3. **Cookie Handling**: Simplifies JWT cookie management
4. **Error Transformation**: Standardize error responses

## Request/Response Interceptors

### Request Interceptor

Located in `src/lib/api/interceptors.ts`:

- Adds request ID for debugging (dev only)
- Logs outgoing requests (dev only)
- Can add custom headers

### Response Interceptor

- Logs responses (dev only)
- Transforms data if needed
- Error handling:
  - 401: Redirect to login
  - 403: Log permission denied
  - 500: Log server error
  - Transforms to standard `ApiError` format

## Type Definitions

### API Response Types

Define all API types in `src/types/api/`:

```typescript
// Common types
export interface PaginatedResponse<T> {
  data: T[];
  total: number;
  page: number;
  limit: number;
}

export interface ApiResponse<T> {
  success: boolean;
  message: string;
  data: T;
}

export interface ApiError {
  success: false;
  message: string;
  code?: string;
  details?: Record<string, any>;
}

// Resource-specific types
export interface User {
  id: string;
  email: string;
  firstName: string;
  lastName: string;
  role: UserRole;
  createdAt: string;
  updatedAt: string;
}

export interface CreateUserPayload {
  email: string;
  password: string;
  firstName: string;
  lastName: string;
  role?: UserRole;
}
```

## TanStack Query Integration

### Query Hook Pattern

```typescript
export function useUsers(
  filters: UserFilters = {},
  options?: Omit<UseQueryOptions<PaginatedResponse<User>>, 'queryKey' | 'queryFn'>
) {
  return useQuery<PaginatedResponse<User>>({
    queryKey: queryKeys.users.list(filters),
    queryFn: async () => {
      const { data } = await apiClient.get(API_ENDPOINTS.USERS.LIST, {
        params: filters,
      });
      return data;
    },
    staleTime: 5 * 60 * 1000,
    gcTime: 10 * 60 * 1000,
    ...options,
  });
}
```

### Mutation Hook Pattern

```typescript
export function useCreateUser(
  options?: Omit<UseMutationOptions<User, ApiError, CreateUserPayload>, 'mutationFn'>
) {
  const queryClient = useQueryClient();

  return useMutation<User, ApiError, CreateUserPayload>({
    mutationFn: async (payload) => {
      const { data } = await apiClient.post(API_ENDPOINTS.USERS.CREATE, payload);
      return data;
    },
    onSuccess: (data) => {
      queryClient.invalidateQueries({ queryKey: queryKeys.users.lists() });
      toast.success('User created successfully');
    },
    onError: (error) => {
      toast.error('Failed to create user', {
        description: error.message,
      });
    },
    ...options,
  });
}
```

## Error Handling Best Practices

### In Hooks

- Always show toast notifications for mutations
- Transform backend errors to user-friendly messages
- Include error details when helpful

### In Components

- Use isError and error from query hooks
- Display appropriate error UI
- Provide retry actions when applicable

```typescript
const { data, isLoading, isError, error } = useUsers(filters);

if (isError) {
  return (
    <ErrorState
      title="Failed to load users"
      message={error?.message}
      onRetry={() => refetch()}
    />
  );
}
```

## Authentication

### JWT Cookie Pattern

- Backend sets HTTP-only cookie on login
- Cookie automatically sent with all requests (withCredentials: true)
- No manual token management needed in frontend
- Logout clears the cookie

### Auth Check

```typescript
export function useAuthUser() {
  return useQuery({
    queryKey: queryKeys.auth.me,
    queryFn: async () => {
      const { data } = await apiClient.get(API_ENDPOINTS.AUTH.ME);
      return data;
    },
    retry: false, // Don't retry auth requests
  });
}
```

## Caching Strategy

### Query Configuration

- **staleTime**: 5 minutes (how long data is considered fresh)
- **gcTime**: 10 minutes (how long unused data stays in cache)
- **retry**: 3 attempts with exponential backoff
- **refetchOnWindowFocus**: false (avoid unnecessary requests)

### When to Invalidate

- After mutations: Invalidate related queries
- On manual refresh: User-initiated
- After auth state change: Clear all caches

```typescript
// After creating a user
queryClient.invalidateQueries({ queryKey: queryKeys.users.lists() });

// After logout
queryClient.clear();
```
